{
 "regions": [
  {
   "id": "r3",
   "type": "stanza_note",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "St. LXVI.—आस्था comp. St. 30 जगज्जाल = all this net-like",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "world.—Mandâkrântâ.",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  {
   "id": "r4",
   "type": "stanza_note",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "St. LXVII.—प्रभाचोर = a common expression comp. सरोरुहद्युतिमुषः",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "in the Ratnâvali Act I., ad finem. स्मरकुसुमबाणव्यतिकरज्वरज्वाला = the",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "blaze of the fever produced from contact with the flowery arrows",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 4,
     "text": "of Cupid. वराकी = poor girl, here a word of commiseration (as in",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 5,
     "text": "Vîracharita p. 78); also a term of contempt.—S'ikhariṇî.",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  {
   "id": "r5",
   "type": "stanza_note",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "St. LVIII.—गेय = गीत. दीपाङ्कुर comp. दंष्ट्राङ्कुर (Nîtis'ataka); but",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "this is more appropriate, meaning a small light. छाया = flame;",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "आतपप्रत्यनीका says Râmarshi, of which I cannot see the application",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 4,
     "text": "here. आकलप्य comp. Kâdambarî p. 7. On सन्तः Râmarshi gives a",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 5,
     "text": "long list of old princes as Bharata, Dilîpa, Raghu &c. The Stanza",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 6,
     "text": "occurs at p. 308 of the Kâvyasangraha.—S'ârdûlavikrîḍita.",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  {
   "id": "r6",
   "type": "stanza_note",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "St. LXIX.—पवनवश is better than वशपवन. आनर्तित = भ्रमित",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "(Râmarshi.) It refers to the eyebrows being sometimes raised",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "and sometimes folded into wrinkles out of pride or conceit.—",
     "end": "join"
    },
    {
     "n": 4,
     "text": "Sragdharâ.",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  {
   "id": "r7",
   "type": "stanza_note",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "St. LXX.—कणशीकर = कणास्तेषामपि शीकराः अत्यल्पकणाः (Râmarshi.)",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "As to Vidyâdharas haunting the Himâlaya see Kumâra. cantos I.",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "and VI. सावमानं यथास्यात्तथा…रताः; सावमानाः (Râmarshi).—Vasantatilakâ.",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  {
   "id": "r8",
   "type": "stanza_note",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "St. LXXI.—यदा. Comp. Nîtis'ataka St. 95. The Samudras are",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "thus given by Râmarshi क्षीरोद, इक्षुरसोद, सुरोद, घृतोद, दधिमन्थोद,",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "क्षारोद, शुद्धोद. निकर = collection St. 52. अन्त = रसातल (Râmarshi); I",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 4,
     "text": "know of no authority for this and though the usual sense",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 5,
     "text": "‘destruction’ has not as much propriety, I think it is the only",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 6,
     "text": "one admissible. धरणिधर = शेष or पर्वत (Râmarshi); with the former",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 7,
     "text": "पाद = पादा इव चरणा इव प्रतीयमाना ये हस्ताः (sic). But the latter, पर्वत,",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 8,
     "text": "ought alone to be adopted. For the idea of the mountains",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 9,
     "text": "supporting the Earth see Kumâra. VI., 68.—S'ikhariṇî.",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
